## Reviews

### Snapshot #1, reviewer "Review · Grok medium", grok grok-4.7: done

A write that points a column at a CONTENT row now has to be able to read that row first, unless the server attests that this request supplied those exact bytes. The attestation is an unexported field on the edit, set by photo, flyer, pronunciation, and wiki saves (including when deduplication reuses a private row), and a query batch cannot send it. System jobs and super admins skip the check. Tests cover publishing someone else's original, re-encode, crop, or thumbnail, reusing bytes the caller actually uploaded, and rejecting a client-supplied attestation.

No significant findings.
